 Now how do you actually pay for all this? So option one is the bring your own keys that I mentioned

00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:09.280
 before. You've got your own account with the providers, you own the contract, they bill you

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:13.520
 and the key lives in the gateway like we saw earlier. Option two that Cloudflare provides is

00:00:13.520 --> 00:00:19.120
 Unified Billing. So Unified Billing is this idea where you load your credits into your Cloudflare

00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:25.200
 account and the gateway pays the provider for you. You've got one relationship with Cloudflare and

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:28.720
 you don't have to set up an account with every provider to start using their models and start

00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:34.480
 taking advantage of the new models that they offer. Credit purchases carry a 5% fee, provider

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:40.160
 rates are passed through with no markup. So each request is paid in one way: your own provider

00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:44.640
 key, or your Cloudflare credits, never both. One more thing I want to look at under settings is the

